    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Discerning house-hunters are in for a treat with the arrival of no.5 Strangford Road East to the market. This handsome double-fronted three-bedroom residence was fully renovated and refurbished (c.2015) from top to bottom, both inside and out. The works included complete rewiring and replumbing, a new roof and triple-glazed windows throughout, so the new owners can simply move in and enjoy.\r\n\r\nAt the heart of this home lies a bright and spacious open-plan kitchen/dining/family room, created through a modern extension. The kitchen comes fully equipped, with the oven, hob, fridge freezer, microwave, dishwasher, washing machine and tumble dryer all included in the sale. The renovation also introduced a dedicated utility room just off the kitchen with additional fitted storage, and a downstairs guest toilet off the entrance hall. A generous reception-style living room features an original fireplace. Upstairs, the accommodation comprises three good-sized bedrooms and a well-appointed family bathroom. Neat storage has been built in under the stairs and in the attic, and the property is fitted with an alarm system.\r\n\r\nOverall, the living accommodation extends to c.125.79 m² / 1354 ft² and is presented in excellent decorative condition throughout. Contemporary finishes and fittings have been carefully chosen to blend harmoniously with the original character of the property, resulting in a family home that feels both modern and traditional in equal measure. \r\n\r\nOutside, the private front garden incorporates a paved driveway for convenient off-street parking with an EV charger, along with a gated pedestrian entrance and side passage access. The south-facing rear garden is a complete suntrap and is neatly landscaped with raised flower beds and patio paving. It also benefits from a fully covered outdoor utility space, ideal for barbecuing and additional storage, and usable all year round whatever the weather.\r\n\r\nStrangford Road East is located within the mature, close-knit residential community of East Wall, on the cusp of the thriving Docklands quarter and IFSC. East Wall has undergone a period of regeneration with hotels, a multi-screen cinema and several supermarkets on its doorstep, and numerous cafés, restaurants and bars within a ten-minute stroll. The 3Arena and Point Square are close by for concerts and entertainment. For fresh air, Fairview Park and the banks of the Tolka are a short walk away, while the Clontarf seafront and its coastal cycleway are within easy reach. East Point Business Park is a fifteen-minute walk from the house and the city centre can be reached on foot in about twenty minutes.\r\n\r\nEast Wall benefits from excellent transport connectivity, with a number of bus routes serving the area in addition to Connolly Station for mainline and DART commuter trains and Luas. Both the East Link Bridge and Port Tunnel (15 minutes to Dublin Airport) are within a 5-minute drive."
      },
